**fossil-fuels** — BLANK (`direction-only`)

The one source is the chaptered text of SB 1137 (2021-2022), authored by Gonzalez ("SB 1137, Gonzalez."), approved 2022-09-16 — a `record` / `author` passage, `own-act`, `in-term`.

Its operative section bars new drilling approvals only inside a health protection zone: "the division shall not approve any notice of intention under Section 3203 within a health protection zone" — i.e. within 3,200 feet of a sensitive receptor. That's `on-question` (it restricts drilling permits, the dimension the rungs order) but the instrument is narrower than any rung: rung 2 ("Allow no new drilling and let production decline over time") is statewide, and rung 1 is a full phase-out. No rung names a setback, so `v4_shape = direction-only` and the row gets no chair. `needs_source` asks for a statewide-scope instrument or her own first-person words on ending new drilling.

No quotes: the bill text is not her words, so there is no candidate quote in the sources.
